    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0424" n="1384" xml:id="pg1384"/>

                <head>No. 928.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Lewis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 4,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your attention is recalled to my No. 68 of
                    December 7 last concerning the complaint of F. C. Butman, of Boston, alleging
                    discrimination by the Portuguese Government against the direct trade between the
                    United States and the Cape Verde Islands as compared with that passing <hi
                        rendition="#italic">via</hi> Lisbon.</p>
                <p>The Department desires to receive as soon as possible the report which my No. 68
                    instructs you to make.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
